      "problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x+3}+4?$",
      "worked_solution": "To obtain the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x+3}+4,$ we can perform the following transformations:\n\n- Take the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Translate the graph to the left by $3$ units to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x+3}.$\n\n- Translate the result up by $4$ units to get the graph of $y=\\sqrt{x+3}+4.$\n\nThe result is the solid blue curve shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14238243/assets/07838d780998cbf654b02601c649b2548c8421533d1e1bb9ef982d025632d965.png)",
